Package: fastrdp-broker
Architecture: all
Depends:
 libpam-modules,
 libpam-runtime,
 libpam0g,
 openssl,
 python3 (>= 3.11),
 systemd,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
Recommends:
 krb5-user,
 libpam-fastrdp-token,
 libpam-sss,
Suggests:
 fastrdp-proxy-module,
 fastrdp-session,
 fastrdp-webgate,
Description: session broker for the fastrdp multi-user RDP terminal server
 fastrdp turns a Linux host into a multi-user RDP terminal server:
 freerdp-proxy3 is the single front end, a session broker decides which
 back end (xrdp, GNOME Remote Desktop, KRdp) a user gets, and one-time
 tokens let the back ends accept only broker-approved logins.
 .
 This package contains fastrdp-brokerd (Python, standard library only),
 the fastrdpctl admin command, the systemd unit, the PAM service used for
 password and account checks, and a default /etc/fastrdp/broker.toml (realm
 and SSSD domains from the host's krb5.conf and sssd.conf). It also has
 the TERMSRV keytab helpers: fastrdp-termsrv-check (AES keys for NLA) and
 fastrdp-termsrv-keytab with a path unit that copies the TERMSRV keys for
 the proxy whenever Active Directory rotates the machine password, the host
 check fastrdp-check-host and fastrdp-defaults, which installs the default
 configuration of the fastrdp packages and keeps local changes on upgrades.
 .
 The services are installed disabled; check /etc/fastrdp/broker.toml,
 then enable fastrdp-brokerd.service (and on AD hosts
 fastrdp-termsrv-keytab.path). Install fastrdp-server for the whole server.

Package: fastrdp-proxy-module
Architecture: any
Depends:
 fastrdp-broker (= ${source:Version}),
 ${fastrdp:FreeRDP},
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: freerdp-proxy3 module that asks the fastrdp broker
 fastrdp turns a Linux host into a multi-user RDP terminal server with
 freerdp-proxy3 as the single front end.
 .
 This package contains the proxy module (loaded with "Modules = fastrdp"),
 which asks fastrdp-brokerd before letting a client in and routes it to its
 back-end session, plus the fastrdp-proxy.service unit that runs
 /opt/fastrdp/bin/freerdp-proxy as the unprivileged _fastrdp-proxy user, a
 default /etc/fastrdp/proxy.ini and fastrdp-front-cert, which creates a
 self-signed front certificate at the first start when none is there.
 .
 The module is built against fastrdp's own FreeRDP build (fastrdp-freerdp3,
 /opt/fastrdp) and requires exactly that FreeRDP release.

Package: libpam-fastrdp-token
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: admin
Depends:
 libpam-runtime,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: PAM module that accepts one-time fastrdp broker tokens
 fastrdp turns a Linux host into a multi-user RDP terminal server.
 .
 pam_fastrdp_token.so lets a back end such as xrdp-sesman accept only
 one-time tokens issued by fastrdp-brokerd. When the broker knows the
 user's password it hands it on to the next module (for example pam_sss),
 so the session still gets a Kerberos ticket.

Package: fastrdp-session
Architecture: all
Depends:
 fastrdp-broker (= ${source:Version}),
 python3,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
Recommends:
 libnotify-bin,
Suggests:
 pipewire-module-xrdp,
Description: session launchers and units for fastrdp back ends
 fastrdp turns a Linux host into a multi-user RDP terminal server.
 .
 This package contains the session side:
  - startwm.sh for xrdp (starts the desktop chosen by the broker),
  - the headless Plasma (Wayland) launcher, its unit template and PAM stack,
  - the KWin virtual-backend drop-in for plasma-kwin_wayland.service,
  - the wlroots-in-x launcher, clipboard bridge and X session entries for
    Sway, labwc and Wayfire,
  - with fastrdp-xrdp: fastrdp's xrdp configuration (xrdp.ini, sesman.ini,
    gfx.toml, xorg.conf, startwm.sh) and the xrdp-sesman PAM stack that
    accepts only broker tokens, installed by fastrdp-defaults in place of
    upstream's versions (local changes are kept),
  - tgt-notify, started in every desktop session (XDG autostart): a desktop
    notification before the session's Kerberos login can no longer be
    renewed (settings: /etc/fastrdp/tgt-notify.conf),
  - xrdp-audio, started in xrdp sessions (XDG autostart, wlroots-in-x): loads
    the PipeWire xrdp module of pipewire-module-xrdp, sink-only when the
    microphone is switched off.

Package: fastrdp-webgate
Architecture: all
Depends:
 fastrdp-broker (= ${source:Version}),
 python3 (>= 3.11),
 python3-cryptography,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
Recommends:
 nginx,
Suggests:
 podman,
Description: browser access gateway for fastrdp (OIDC login to Guacamole)
 fastrdp turns a Linux host into a multi-user RDP terminal server.
 .
 fastrdp-webgate logs users in with an OpenID Connect provider (for example
 Keycloak), asks fastrdp-brokerd for a one-time token and hands an encrypted
 connection to Apache Guacamole, which connects through the fastrdp proxy.
 .
 The service is installed disabled; configure /etc/fastrdp/webgate.toml,
 then enable fastrdp-webgate.service.

Package: fastrdp-server
Architecture: all
Depends:
