 realmd,
 sssd,
 sssd-kcm,
 sssd-tools,
Suggests:
 fastrdp-webgate,
Description: fastrdp multi-user RDP terminal server (complete host)
 fastrdp turns a Linux host into a multi-user RDP terminal server:
 freerdp-proxy3 is the single front end, a session broker decides which
 back end (xrdp, GNOME Remote Desktop, KRdp) a user gets.
 .
 Installing this package sets up the host as the Ansible roles do with their
 defaults: all fastrdp packages and the base packages, fastrdp-firewall.service
 (nftables: only the proxy may reach the back-end ports), the back-end ports
 kept out of the ephemeral range, TCP tuning (BBR), no power actions from RDP
 sessions (polkit), per-user resource limits, and the Kerberos (KCM, renewable
 tickets) and SSSD (ticket renewal) client settings. The files in /usr can be
 overridden with the same name below /etc; those in /etc are fastrdp-defaults
 files (local changes are kept).
 .
 The remaining steps (domain join, desktops, starting the services) are in
 docs/manual-setup.md; fastrdp-check-host --preflight checks the host first.

Package: fastrdp-archive-keyring
Architecture: all
Section: misc
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: OpenPGP key and APT source of the fast-rdp-server repository
 fastrdp turns a Linux host into a multi-user RDP terminal server.
 .
 This package contains the key that signs the fast-rdp-server APT repository
 (https://linuxrrze.github.io/fast-rdp-server) in /usr/share/keyrings and, when
 no source for it is configured yet, adds
 /etc/apt/sources.list.d/fast-rdp-server.sources for this release's stable
 channel. Download it once from the repository and install it with apt; later
 key changes then arrive as updates.
